{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"150","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Quantity of Strings"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Just in case somebody missed it: this winter is totally cold in Nvodsk! It is so cold that one gets funny thoughts. For example, let's say there are strings with the length exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", based on the alphabet of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":". Any its substring with length equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a palindrome. How many such strings exist? Your task is to find their quantity modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Be careful and don't miss a string or two!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let us remind you that a string is a palindrome if it can be read the same way in either direction, from the left to the right and from the right to the left."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and only line contains three integers: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, m, k ≤ 2000"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the number of strings of the described type modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 2 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample only one string is valid: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (let's denote the only letter of our alphabet as \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample (if we denote the alphabet letters as \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\") the following strings are valid: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aaaaa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bbbbb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"150B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/150/problem/B"}